    {
      "_id": "Hn5PgfCFMwbKdN20",
      "effects": [],
      "flags": {},
      "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp",
      "name": "Self-Loathing",
      "sort": 400000,
      "type": "action",
      "folder": null,
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "<p>If a revenant sees their own reflection or any object that was important to them in life, they must attempt a @Check[type:will|dc:25] save.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The revenant is unaffected and can no longer be affected by that reflection or object in this way.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The revenant is distracted by self-loathing and becomes @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 1} for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The revenant becomes @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.AdPVz7rbaVSRxHFg]{Fascinated} by the source that triggered their self-loathing and does everything they can to destroy it until the end of the revenant's next turn.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The revenant becomes @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.eIcWbB5o3pP6OIMe]{Immobilized} as long as the source of their self-loathing is apparent, until they're attacked, or until they see their murderer.</p>"
        },
        "source": {
